need you to do a thorough review of the code base. looking for anything that might be benefecial to get the most performace out of the machine.

i need a good way to get audio monitoring on a second audio output (system audio) so i can monitor each channel or input by soloing it in the audio mixer.

i also see some micro stuters on screen consumer. the weird thing is that the same channel in the operator gui is smooth, yet on the actual output it stutters a little.

live inputs need to have a blue label bar (not red) under them in compose preview.
the pgm has capture button and others have prt should be unified.

the test pattern displays the resolution twice at the top.
now it displays it once ate the top and then the second time after screen consumer. once at the top is enough.
the boucing character has too big "bump box", meaning on the left and right it bounces of the wall too early, not when the character actually touches the border.


the prv channels need to appear in audio mixer, so operators can monitor the audio of video before taking it to pgm.


you added the usb headphones as a second portaudio output, which i dont think is possible. thats why i explicitly said to use system audio for this.
tried listenting to a prv channel and its just weird stuttery noise.

the bouncing character needs to have relative size to the size of the screen, right now on smaller screen its too big.

usb drives auto mount doesnt work. its neccesery so operators can plug a drive in and import media without going into terminal to mount it. it needs to support multiple drives/mounts.

i need you to look over the gui and remove stupid notes. like under the audio mixer console, "full tcatile..."
and others. most of the stuff is selfexplanatory no need for notes.

then i need a full code base review

in a couple places there is a subtitle of highascg as broadcast playout graphics. or direct playout.
i want all of them to say media server. the titile of the browser tab also says it.

tried running eggs produce and flash to drive, then i ran it on a different machine and ran the calamares installer (also the above in the installer) and the installer failed to install with failed to install boot loader.


